  message: "Dogfood CORRECTION reopen (member F148.A1) — corrects this invariant's cc-closure, reproduces on the frozen substrate. The bash cyclomatic_complexity gap is still present: bash symbols carry lines_of_code (71%) but cyclomatic_complexity remains 0% populated, contradicting the closure note \"Satisfied via PR1 + PR5 sweeps across 10 mainstream analyzers.\" The dogfood pass found bash cc% = 0 on the substrate. This invariant is currently already in the violated state (it had been reopened previously), so no further status change is required — recording this finding to keep the bash cyclomatic_complexity gap explicit under the invariant per the status-adjustment rule. Note for contrast: the Python cyclomatic_complexity OVER-count of `with` statements (a distinct defect, populated-but-wrong rather than absent) is filed as a separate net-new row (WI-gapir, F158.A1). Cross-ref WI-gapir."  # a0d4
